IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc32-related-2`

-- ccc32-tests-related-2.l4 -- tests for ccc32-related-2.l4 (2018 c. 12 s. 406 to 2023 c. 32 s. 14.1).
-- Every expected value is decided by reading the provision, and written beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The days are made-up days (the commencement days are not in the sources); the arithmetic on them is calendar arithmetic done by hand.

`ccc32 test section 499` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 499, ""
`ccc32 test section 498` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 498, ""
`ccc32 test section 500` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 500, ""
`ccc32 test subsection 503(2)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 503, "(2)"
`ccc32 test subsection 503(2.1)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 503, "(2.1)"
`ccc32 test subsection 503(3.1)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 503, "(3.1)"
`ccc32 test section 515` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 515, ""
`ccc32 test section 597` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 597, ""
`ccc32 test section 679` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 679, ""
`ccc32 test section 832` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 832, ""

§ `2018 c. 12 s. 406`

-- Section 404 came into force on 1 January 2019 (a made-up day). "before the day": 31 December 2018 yes; the day itself no (not covered, never FALSE).
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(1) a remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of the offence` (Date 1 1 2019) (Date 31 12 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(1) a remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of the offence` (Date 1 1 2019) (Date 1 1 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(1) a remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of the offence` (Date 1 1 2019) (Date 2 1 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) the meaning is section 715.3's: its answer is carried through, NOTHING included; another term is not covered.
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(2) the term has the meaning it has in section 715.3` `2018 c 12 s 406(2) remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(2) the term has the meaning it has in section 715.3` `2018 c 12 s 406(2) offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(2) the term has the meaning it has in section 715.3` `2018 c 12 s 406(2) offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2018 c 12 s 406(2) the term has the meaning it has in section 715.3` `2018 c 12 s 406(2) another term` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

