§ `2019 c. 25 s. 359 -- the right to re-elect`

-- The trial is first appointed for 1 June 2020; "not later than 14 days before" is 18 May 2020 at the latest.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 18 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one day later, no consent: the text's period says no; with the prosecutor's written consent (also after the trial date): yes.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 19 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 19 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 2 6 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if they have not already done so": already elected -> the text's no. Not accused before the day, or not in one of the cases: not covered.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power and its failed "if" gate is the text's limit on the grant, not the text's no, so the answer is NOTHING (name-test sweep, fork F25) (only the "if they have not already done so" branch; the 14-day deadline branch keeps JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- whether the person is in one of the cases of section 561 is another part's answer: not covered stays not covered.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` TRUE NOTHING FALSE (Date 17 5 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2019 c. 25 s. 360 -- the six-month limit for offences punishable on summary conviction committed before section 315 came into force`

-- Section 315 came into force on 1 January 2020 (made up). Subject matter arose 15 January 2019: six months on is 15 July 2019.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 7 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 15 1 2019) (Date 15 7 2019) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 7 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 15 1 2019) (Date 16 7 2019) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- by agreement of the prosecutor and the defendant ("unless ... so agree"): within, even after six months.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 7 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 15 1 2019) (Date 16 7 2019) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Subject matter arose 31 August 2019: `add months` clamps six months on to 29 February 2020 (finding, fork F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 9 2019) (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 31 8 2019) (Date 29 2 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 9 2019) (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 31 8 2019) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- outside the section's scope: committed on or after the day section 315 came into force, or not punishable on summary conviction.
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 15 1 2019) (Date 16 7 2019) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` FALSE (Date 1 7 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 15 1 2019) (Date 16 7 2019) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

